<p style="text-align: center;"><img src="/images/2015/49ers.jpg" alt="Drawing in graphite of two children" width="450" height="579" /></p>
<p style="text-align: center;">49ers. 20x16, pencil on hot press watercolor paper. 2015</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Starting with a grainy cell-phone photograph I created this figurative portrait by reducing the picture to about 4 values and eliminating as much of the background clutter as possible.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;"><span style="line-height: 1.42857143;">As usual, I laid down the drawing in a series of layers: a light block-in, the main values&nbsp;</span><span style="line-height: 1.42857143;">(dark, dark middle tone, light middle tone and light), with edge work</span><span style="line-height: 1.42857143;">&nbsp;and balancing of the tones to finish.</span></p>